IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 4 (sections 137ZD to 137ZG): the civil penalty. The Authority acts only with the consent of the Public Prosecutor and the court makes the order,
-- so each function answers what the Act lets be done or bars; the person who is on the receiving end asks the question in the seat layer.
-- "Whenever it appears to the Authority" and "with the consent of the Public Prosecutor" gate a "may": SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork lines B12 and B13.

§ `s 137ZD: civil penalty`

-- The provisions section 137ZD(1)(a) lists, one constructor each (paragraph (a)(i) names sixteen sections, (a)(ii) and (a)(iii) the Division 1 provisions as applied), and one for any other provision.
DECLARE `s 137ZD(1)(a) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 133(1) or (3)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 135`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 136(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137A`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137B`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137F(5)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137G(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137M(5)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137N(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137P(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137R(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137X(5)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137Y(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137ZA(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(i) section 137ZC(1) or (2)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(ii) section 135, 136, 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137J(1)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a)(iii) section 135, 136, 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(a) a provision the paragraph does not list`

-- The provisions section 137ZD(1)(b) lists: paragraph (b)(i) names fifteen sections (whole sections, not subsections, apart from 137F(5) and 137M(5) and 137X(5)), (b)(ii) and (b)(iii) the as-applied provisions.
DECLARE `s 137ZD(1)(b) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 133`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 135`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 136`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137B`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137F(5)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137G`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137M(5)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137N`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137P`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137R`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137X(5)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137Y`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137ZA`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(i) section 137ZC`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(ii) section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137J(1)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b)(iii) section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)`
    `s 137ZD(1)(b) a provision the paragraph does not list`

-- src:30897 | 137ZD.—(1) Whenever it appears to the Authority that any person
-- src:30898 | has —
-- src:30903 | (a) intentionally or recklessly, contravened any of the
-- src:30904 | following provisions:
-- src:30906 | (i) section 133(1) or (3), 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A,
-- src:30907 | 137B, 137F(5), 137G(1) or (2), 137M(5), 137N(1) or
-- src:30908 | (2), 137P(1) or (2), 137R(1) or (2), 137X(5),
-- src:30909 | 137Y(1) or (2), 137ZA(1) or (2) or 137ZC(1) or (2);
-- src:30911 | (ii) section 135, 136, 137, 137A or 137B as applied by
-- src:30912 | section 137J(1);
-- src:30914 | (iii) section 135, 136, 137, 137A or 137B as applied by
-- src:30915 | section 137U(1);
@ref s 137ZD(1)(a) (src:30897-30915)
GIVEN
    `the provision contravened under section 137ZD(1)(a)` IS A `s 137ZD(1)(a) provision` @desc Which provision did the person contravene (one of those section 137ZD(1)(a) lists, or another)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(1)(a) the person intentionally or recklessly contravened a provision the paragraph lists` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision contravened under section 137ZD(1)(a)` EQUALS `s 137ZD(1)(a) a provision the paragraph does not list`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "contravened any of the following provisions"; the provision is not among them
        IF `the contravention was intentional or reckless`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says which contraventions found a civil action ("intentionally or recklessly, contravened"), not that any other contravention is free of one

-- src:30917 | (b) in purported compliance with any of the following
-- src:30918 | provisions, provided, announced or disseminated any
-- src:30919 | information which the person knows is false or
-- src:30920 | misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to
-- src:30921 | whether it is:
-- src:30923 | (i) section 133, 135, 136, 137, 137B, 137F(5), 137G,
-- src:30924 | 137M(5), 137N, 137P, 137R, 137X(5), 137Y, 137ZA
-- src:30925 | or 137ZC;
-- src:30927 | (ii) section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by
-- src:30928 | section 137J(1);
-- src:30930 | (iii) section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by
-- src:30931 | section 137U(1); or
@ref s 137ZD(1)(b) (src:30917-30931)
GIVEN
    `the provision complied with under section 137ZD(1)(b)` IS A `s 137ZD(1)(b) provision` @desc In purported compliance with which provision did the person provide, announce or disseminate the information (one of those section 137ZD(1)(b) lists, or another)?
    `the person provided, announced or disseminated information in purported compliance that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with the provision, did the person provide, announce or disseminate information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(1)(b) the person gave false or misleading information in purported compliance with a provision the paragraph lists` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision complied with under section 137ZD(1)(b)` EQUALS `s 137ZD(1)(b) a provision the paragraph does not list`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "in purported compliance with any of the following provisions"; the provision is not among them
        IF `the person provided, announced or disseminated information in purported compliance that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says which false or misleading information founds a civil action ("which the person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that any other is free of one

-- src:30933 | (c) being an officer of a corporation to which Division 1
-- src:30934 | applies, an officer of a trustee‑manager of a registered or
-- src:30935 | recognised business trust to which Division 2 applies, or an
-- src:30936 | officer of a responsible person for a real estate investment
-- src:30937 | trust to which Division 3 applies, intentionally or
-- src:30938 | recklessly committed an act referred to in
-- src:30939 | subsection (5)(a), (b) or (c) of section 137G, 137R or
-- src:30940 | 137ZC, as the case may be,
@ref s 137ZD(1)(c) (src:30933-30940)
GIVEN
    `the person is an officer of a corporation to which Division 1 applies, of a trustee-manager to which Division 2 applies, or of a responsible person to which Division 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer of a corporation to which Division 1 applies, of the trustee-manager of a registered or recognised business trust to which Division 2 applies, or of a responsible person for a real estate investment trust to which Division 3 applies?
    `the person committed an act referred to in section 137G(5)(a), (b) or (c), 137R(5)(a), (b) or (c) or 137ZC(5)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person commit an act referred to in section 137G(5)(a), (b) or (c), section 137R(5)(a), (b) or (c) or section 137ZC(5)(a), (b) or (c) (as the case may be)?
    `the person acted intentionally or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person act intentionally or recklessly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(1)(c) the officer intentionally or recklessly committed an act referred to in the paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer of a corporation to which Division 1 applies, of a trustee-manager to which Division 2 applies, or of a responsible person to which Division 3 applies` AND `the person committed an act referred to in section 137G(5)(a), (b) or (c), 137R(5)(a), (b) or (c) or 137ZC(5)(a), (b) or (c)` AND `the person acted intentionally or recklessly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who founds a civil action ("being an officer of a corporation to which Division 1 applies ... intentionally or recklessly committed an act"), not that anyone else is free of one

-- The Authority's power: "Whenever it appears to the Authority that any person has" done an act of paragraph (a), (b) or (c), "the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action".
-- A "may" gated by "Whenever" (which counts as "where") and by a consent: the grant limit of the ruling of 2026-11-12 answers NOTHING when a gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would answer JUST FALSE.
-- SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork lines B12 (the "Whenever" gate) and B13 (the consent).
-- src:30897 | 137ZD.—(1) Whenever it appears to the Authority that any person
-- src:30898 | has —
-- src:30903 | (a) intentionally or recklessly, contravened any of the
-- src:30904 | following provisions:
-- src:30906 | (i) section 133(1) or (3), 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A,
-- src:30907 | 137B, 137F(5), 137G(1) or (2), 137M(5), 137N(1) or
-- src:30908 | (2), 137P(1) or (2), 137R(1) or (2), 137X(5),
-- src:30909 | 137Y(1) or (2), 137ZA(1) or (2) or 137ZC(1) or (2);
-- src:30911 | (ii) section 135, 136, 137, 137A or 137B as applied by
-- src:30912 | section 137J(1);
-- src:30914 | (iii) section 135, 136, 137, 137A or 137B as applied by
-- src:30915 | section 137U(1);
-- src:30917 | (b) in purported compliance with any of the following
-- src:30918 | provisions, provided, announced or disseminated any
-- src:30919 | information which the person knows is false or
-- src:30920 | misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to
-- src:30921 | whether it is:
-- src:30923 | (i) section 133, 135, 136, 137, 137B, 137F(5), 137G,
-- src:30924 | 137M(5), 137N, 137P, 137R, 137X(5), 137Y, 137ZA
-- src:30925 | or 137ZC;
-- src:30927 | (ii) section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by
-- src:30928 | section 137J(1);
-- src:30930 | (iii) section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by
-- src:30931 | section 137U(1); or
-- src:30933 | (c) being an officer of a corporation to which Division 1
-- src:30934 | applies, an officer of a trustee‑manager of a registered or
-- src:30935 | recognised business trust to which Division 2 applies, or an
-- src:30936 | officer of a responsible person for a real estate investment
-- src:30937 | trust to which Division 3 applies, intentionally or
-- src:30938 | recklessly committed an act referred to in
-- src:30939 | subsection (5)(a), (b) or (c) of section 137G, 137R or
-- src:30940 | 137ZC, as the case may be,
-- src:30942 | the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an
-- src:30943 | action in a court against the person to seek an order for a civil penalty
-- src:30944 | in respect of that act.
@ref s 137ZD(1) (src:30897-30944)
GIVEN
    `the person has done an act in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of section 137ZD(1) as the Authority's reading` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for the paragraph answer for the person? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `it appears to the Authority that the person has done an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Authority that the person has done an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)?
    `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the Authority's bringing the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(1) the Authority may bring an action in a court for an order for a civil penalty` MEANS
    IF (`the person has done an act in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of section 137ZD(1) as the Authority's reading` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `it appears to the Authority that the person has done an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` AND `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Whenever it appears to the Authority that any person has" ... "the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action in a court against the person to seek an order for a civil penalty in respect of that act"

-- src:30951 | (2) If the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that
-- src:30952 | subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) (as the case may be) has been proved, the
-- src:30953 | court may make an order against the person for the payment of a civil
-- src:30954 | penalty of a sum not less than $50,000 and not more than $2 million.
@ref s 137ZD(2) (src:30951-30954)
GIVEN
    `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c) has been proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c) (as the case may be) has been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(2) the court may make an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c) has been proved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) (as the case may be) has been proved, the court may make an order"

-- The limits: "a sum not less than $50,000 and not more than $2 million". A sum outside them is the text's no ("not less than ... and not more than").
-- src:30951 | (2) If the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that
-- src:30952 | subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) (as the case may be) has been proved, the
-- src:30953 | court may make an order against the person for the payment of a civil
-- src:30954 | penalty of a sum not less than $50,000 and not more than $2 million.
@ref 2 s 137ZD(2) (the limits) (src:30951-30954)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(2) the amount of the civil penalty is within the limits` MEANS
    IF (`the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars` AT LEAST 50000) AND (`the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars` AT MOST 2000000)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a civil penalty of a sum not less than $50,000 and not more than $2 million"

-- src:30958 | (3) Despite subsection (2), the court may make an order against a
-- src:30959 | person against whom an action has been brought under this section if
-- src:30960 | the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has agreed to
-- src:30961 | allow the person to consent to the order with or without admission of
-- src:30962 | having committed an act referred to in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)
-- src:30963 | (whichever is applicable), and the order may be made on such terms
-- src:30964 | as may be agreed between the Authority and the person.
@ref s 137ZD(3) (src:30958-30964)
GIVEN
    `an action has been brought against the person under section 137ZD` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an action been brought against the person under section 137ZD?
    `the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has agreed to allow the person to consent to the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, agreed to allow the person to consent to the order, with or without admission of having committed the act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(3) the court may make an order on the terms agreed between the Authority and the person` MEANS
    IF `an action has been brought against the person under section 137ZD` AND `the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has agreed to allow the person to consent to the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may make an order against a person against whom an action has been brought under this section if the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has agreed to allow the person to consent to the order"

-- Subsection (4) is a flat negative ("Nothing in this section is to be construed to prevent"): it removes an obstacle and grants nothing further. The answer is JUST TRUE for an
-- agreement within the limits of subsection (2) for an act of paragraph (a), (b) or (c); anything else is outside the sentence.
-- src:30968 | (4) Nothing in this section is to be construed to prevent the
-- src:30969 | Authority from entering into an agreement with the person to pay,
-- src:30970 | with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty within the limits
-- src:30971 | referred to in subsection (2) for an act referred to in subsection (1)(a),
-- src:30972 | (b) or (c).
@ref s 137ZD(4) (src:30968-30972)
GIVEN
    `the agreement is for an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement to pay a civil penalty for an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)?
    `the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(4) nothing in section 137ZD prevents the Authority from entering into the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is for an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` AND (`s 137ZD(2) the amount of the civil penalty is within the limits` `the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a civil penalty within the limits referred to in subsection (2) for an act referred to in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)"

-- src:30976 | (5) A civil penalty imposed under this section is to be paid into the
-- src:30977 | Consolidated Fund and is to be treated as a debt due to the
-- src:30978 | Government for the purposes of section 10 of the Government
-- src:30979 | Proceedings Act 1956.
@ref s 137ZD(5) (src:30976-30979)
GIVEN
    `a civil penalty has been imposed under section 137ZD` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a civil penalty been imposed under section 137ZD?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(5) the civil penalty is paid into the Consolidated Fund and is a debt due to the Government` MEANS
    IF `a civil penalty has been imposed under section 137ZD`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A civil penalty imposed under this section"

-- src:30983 | (6) If the person fails to pay the civil penalty imposed on the person
-- src:30984 | within the time specified in the court order referred to in
-- src:30985 | subsection (3) or specified under the agreement referred to in
-- src:30986 | subsection (4), the Authority may recover the civil penalty as though
-- src:30987 | the civil penalty were a judgment debt due to the Authority.
@ref s 137ZD(6) (src:30983-30987)
GIVEN
    `the person fails to pay the civil penalty within the time specified in the court order or under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person failed to pay the civil penalty within the time specified in the court order referred to in section 137ZD(3) or under the agreement referred to in section 137ZD(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(6) the Authority may recover the civil penalty as a judgment debt due to the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to pay the civil penalty within the time specified in the court order or under the agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person fails to pay the civil penalty imposed on the person within the time specified in the court order referred to in subsection (3) or specified under the agreement referred to in subsection (4), the Authority may recover"

-- src:30991 | (7) Any defence that is available to a person who is prosecuted for
-- src:30992 | an act under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), is also available to a person
-- src:30993 | against whom an action is brought under this section for the same act.
@ref s 137ZD(7) (src:30991-30993)
GIVEN
    `a defence is available to a person prosecuted for the act under section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a defence available to a person prosecuted for the act under section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)?
    `an action has been brought against the person under section 137ZD` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an action been brought against the person under section 137ZD?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZD(7) the defence is also available to the person against whom the action is brought` MEANS
    IF `a defence is available to a person prosecuted for the act under section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` AND `an action has been brought against the person under section 137ZD`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any defence that is available to a person who is prosecuted for an act under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), is also available to a person against whom an action is brought under this section for the same act"

§ `s 137ZE: action under section 137ZD not to commence, etc., in certain situations`

-- (1)(a): "must not be commenced against any person" ... "after the expiration of 6 years from the date of the act": a bar, answered JUST TRUE when it applies and JUST FALSE when it does not
-- (marginal reading (b): the bar is limited by its own wording, and outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING). 6 years run from the date of the act (sfa-periods P1, P4).
-- src:31003 | 137ZE.—(1) An action under section 137ZD for an act referred to
-- src:31004 | in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) of that section must not be commenced
-- src:31005 | against any person —
-- src:31007 | (a) after the expiration of 6 years from the date of the act; or
@ref s 137ZE(1)(a) (src:31003-31007)
GIVEN
    `the day of the act` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act done?
    `the day the action is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 137ZD commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZE(1)(a) the action must not be commenced because 6 years from the date of the act have expired` MEANS
    IF `the day the action is commenced` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the act` 6 Years
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced against any person" ... "after the expiration of 6 years from the date of the act"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): the bar is limited by its own wording ("after the expiration of 6 years"); outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING.

-- (1)(b): "if the person has been convicted or acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for that act, except where the person has been acquitted because of the
-- withdrawal of the charge against the person". Convicted: barred. Acquitted: barred unless the acquittal was because the charge was withdrawn.
-- src:31009 | (b) if the person has been convicted or acquitted in criminal
-- src:31010 | proceedings instituted against the person for that act,
-- src:31011 | except where the person has been acquitted because of the
-- src:31012 | withdrawal of the charge against the person.
@ref s 137ZE(1)(b) (src:31009-31012)
GIVEN
    `the person has been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act?
    `the person has been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act?
    `the person was acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge against the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZE(1)(b) the action must not be commenced because the person has been convicted or acquitted` MEANS
    IF `the person has been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` OR (`the person has been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` AND (NOT `the person was acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person has been convicted or acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for that act, except where the person has been acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge against the person"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): the bar is limited by its own wording ("if", "except"); outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING.

-- src:31003 | 137ZE.—(1) An action under section 137ZD for an act referred to
-- src:31004 | in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) of that section must not be commenced
-- src:31005 | against any person —
-- src:31007 | (a) after the expiration of 6 years from the date of the act; or
-- src:31009 | (b) if the person has been convicted or acquitted in criminal
-- src:31010 | proceedings instituted against the person for that act,
-- src:31011 | except where the person has been acquitted because of the
-- src:31012 | withdrawal of the charge against the person.
@ref s 137ZE(1) (src:31003-31012)
GIVEN
    `the day of the act` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act done?
    `the day the action is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 137ZD commenced?
    `the person has been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act?
    `the person has been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act?
    `the person was acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge against the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZE(1) the action must not be commenced` MEANS
    IF (`s 137ZE(1)(a) the action must not be commenced because 6 years from the date of the act have expired` `the day of the act` `the day the action is commenced` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 137ZE(1)(b) the action must not be commenced because the person has been convicted or acquitted` `the person has been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` `the person has been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against the person for the act` `the person was acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced against any person"; neither paragraph applies
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): see paragraphs (a) and (b).

-- (2): the action "must be stayed after criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person for that act, and may thereafter be continued only if" (a) the person has been discharged
-- and the discharge is not an acquittal, or (b) the charge has been withdrawn. "After" limits the stay (NOTHING outside it); "only if" closes the continuation (JUST FALSE outside it).
-- src:31016 | (2) An action under section 137ZD against any person for an act
-- src:31017 | referred to in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) of that section must be
-- src:31018 | stayed after criminal proceedings have been commenced against the
-- src:31019 | person for that act, and may thereafter be continued only if —
-- src:31021 | (a) that person has been discharged in respect of that act and
-- src:31022 | the discharge does not amount to an acquittal; or
-- src:31024 | (b) the charge against that person in respect of that act has been
-- src:31025 | withdrawn.
@ref s 137ZE(2) (src:31016-31025)
GIVEN
    `criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have criminal proceedings been commenced against the person for the act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZE(2) the action must be stayed` MEANS
    IF `criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person for the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be stayed after criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person for that act"

-- src:31016 | (2) An action under section 137ZD against any person for an act
-- src:31017 | referred to in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) of that section must be
-- src:31018 | stayed after criminal proceedings have been commenced against the
-- src:31019 | person for that act, and may thereafter be continued only if —
-- src:31021 | (a) that person has been discharged in respect of that act and
-- src:31022 | the discharge does not amount to an acquittal; or
-- src:31024 | (b) the charge against that person in respect of that act has been
-- src:31025 | withdrawn.
@ref 2 s 137ZE(2) (continuing the action) (src:31016-31025)
GIVEN
    `the person has been discharged in respect of the act and the discharge does not amount to an acquittal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been discharged in respect of the act, and does the discharge not amount to an acquittal?
    `the charge against the person in respect of the act has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the charge against the person in respect of the act been withdrawn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZE(2) the stayed action may be continued` MEANS
    IF `the person has been discharged in respect of the act and the discharge does not amount to an acquittal` OR `the charge against the person in respect of the act has been withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may thereafter be continued only if"

§ `s 137ZF: jurisdiction of the District Court`

-- src:31031 | 137ZF. A District Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine any
-- src:31032 | action under section 137ZD regardless of the monetary amount.
@ref s 137ZF (src:31031-31032)
GIVEN
    `the action under section 137ZD is brought in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action under section 137ZD brought in a District Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137ZF a District Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine the action regardless of the monetary amount` MEANS
    IF `the action under section 137ZD is brought in a District Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A District Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine any action under section 137ZD"

-- s 137ZG (Rules of Court may be made for procedure, costs and fees): a rule-making power, so a coverage row `inert` (reason 2), no code.
